    "id": "unified-example-story-documents",
    "name": "A scene as letters, notices and witness messages",
    "description": "Generate the shared public scene, create three attributed in-world documents, check chronology and audience knowledge, and append the packet as proposed artifacts.\n\nSetup: Bind Prose and decision. The clerk, notice writer and witness each receive only the public native body, with authored author/audience constraints. The clock is supplied as accepted story-time evidence. Private letters need a separate actor grant and must not be appended to this public packet. Statements remain attributed claims; contradictory testimony can be intentional.\n\nInspect: On Send owns this generation. Generate Reply uses the ordinary SillyTavern connection. Auxiliary roles remain unassigned in this portable example. Review the final narrative and proposed consequences; Apply publishes a new swipe and settles staged writes. Preview and bounded runs never settle.\n\nGenerated suggestions are proposals. Quoted observations preserve source identity; notes never establish canonical events. Private records cannot be appended to public notes.",
